vice": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across regions. I retried the rollback and it completed. Current state: all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy, and check the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52760, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CZHhohULacZ9CFRGXqCkyv", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52760, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CZHhohULacZ9CFRGXqCkyv", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 54585, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002). I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the one failing. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across regions. I retried once and it completed across all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback, and the halted first attempt. The first incident request timed out, so I retried it with the same idempotency key; it was created once.\