s after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across regions. I retried the rollback and it completed. Current state: all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy, and check the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002). I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the one failing. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across regions. I retried once and it completed across all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback, and the halted first attempt. The first incident request timed out, so I retried it with the same idempotency key; it was created once.\n\nFollow-ups for the on-call engineer:\n- Investigate the v2.3.1 failure before anyone redeploys it.\n- Check the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "type": "text"}]}]}